{"lens":"completeness_governance","slice":"020H.1","commit":"3817384","verdict":"CONDITIONAL_PASS","fixpoint":true,"summary":"R2 completeness-governance review at commit 3817384 (post fix-round-1). Fixpoint criterion met: zero new CRIT or MAJ findings. All nine R1 closures verified genuine: (a) TF-020H1-001 present in STATUS.md with enforce_release_gate closure path; (b) TF-020H1-002 present with paging-rotation closure path; (c) D-036 filed in DECISIONS.md with all required fields matching D-035 pattern; (d) release:{types:[published]} trigger confirmed in canary-replay.yml lines 32-36; (e) ADOPT-001 §12.7.5 step 4 updated from '(lands in 020H.1)' to file-path + 'shipped at 020H.1'; (f) README.md §Process §2 D-031 citation confirmed as 'per D-031 in `docs/DECISIONS.md`'; (g) TF-020H1-003 auto-defer item present in STATUS.md; (h) TF-020H3-003 closure-path corrected to 'NOT 020H.1'; (i) RULE-TEMPLATE.md §6 extended with SCP-E005 reference, adapter.py path, and merge-blocking consequence. Cumulative document coherence is strong across VERSIONING.md, rule-proposals README+RULE-TEMPLATE, canary-replay.yml, ADOPT-001 §12.7.11, and DECISIONS.md D-036. 020H.2 STATUS.md backfill confirmed at PR #77 commit bac1427. TF-020H1-001..005 all present with credible closure paths; DISPATCH-NOTE 'Out of scope' correctly names all five. No scope drift: fix-round-1 additions (SECURITY.md, bypass-window governance, RULE-TEMPLATE §5 implicit-exclusion set) are direct safety-finding responses, not new feature scope. Three MIN and two nit findings prevent APPROVED verdict: D-036 not in STATUS.md 'Recent decisions' (explicit omission from the R1 COMP-MAJ-003 mitigation's two-part requirement); SCP-073.sec not struck through in STATUS.md despite SECURITY.md shipping in fix-round-1; D-036 not in ADOPT-001 §12.7 References block, breaking the D-029..D-035 per-slice citation pattern.","findings":[{"id":"COMP-R2-MIN-001","severity":"MIN","claim":"D-036 is absent from STATUS.md 'Recent decisions' section despite the R1 COMP-MAJ-003 mitigation explicitly requiring 'Add a STATUS.md Recent decisions row for D-036 (2026-05-01)'. FIX-ROUND-1's COMP-MAJ-003 closure row describes filing D-036 in DECISIONS.md but omits the STATUS.md half of the stated two-part mitigation.","evidence":"STATUS.md 'Recent decisions' section lists D-029 through D-035 (last entry D-035, 2026-04-30) with no D-036 row. docs/DECISIONS.md contains D-036 (date: 2026-05-01) with full content. R1 review-completeness.json COMP-MAJ-003 mitigation (verbatim): 'File D-036 in docs/DECISIONS.md before merge... Add a STATUS.md Recent decisions row for D-036 (2026-05-01).' FIX-ROUND-1 COMP-MAJ-003 row: 'D-036 filed in docs/DECISIONS.md ratifying VERSIONING.md semver contract...' — no mention of STATUS.md update. The prior pattern is unbroken for D-029..D-035: every slice's ratifying decision appears in both DECISIONS.md and STATUS.md Recent decisions.","impact":"STATUS.md 'Recent decisions' is the first-look governance summary for operators and future-slice reviewers. The semver-contract and RFC-process ratification — the most significant governance commitment in this slice, closing WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5 — is invisible at a glance. A reviewer performing a STATUS.md scan to reconstruct the 020H.1 governance record would find no D-036 entry and would need to search DECISIONS.md separately. The omission is an incomplete closure of the COMP-MAJ-003 mitigation.","mitigation":"Add '- **D-036 (2026-05-01)** — VERSIONING.md MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH semver contract with one-release deprecation ramp AND docs/reviews/rule-proposals/ RFC-lite process (quorum=1, 48h wall-clock window, auto-defer on zero approvals, non-waivable window for bypass-introducing proposals) adopted as estate doctrine. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5.' to STATUS.md 'Recent decisions' section before merge."},{"id":"COMP-R2-MIN-002","severity":"MIN","claim":"SCP-073.sec is not marked as landed in STATUS.md 'Post-Threshold-A backlog' despite SECURITY.md being delivered in fix-round-1 (SAFE-MAJ-003 closure). The entry still appears open — no strikethrough, no landed annotation.","evidence":"SECURITY.md repo-root file header (confirmed by read): 'Status: v1.0.0 stub (closes WP-SCP-022 020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-003). Closes: WP-SCP-020 §4.1 follow-up SCP-073.sec.' FIX-ROUND-1 SAFE-MAJ-003 row explicitly states 'Closes WP-SCP-020 §4.1 follow-up SCP-073.sec.' STATUS.md line 133: '- **SCP-073.sec**: `SECURITY.md` publication (security disclosure path for policy-bypass reports) — referenced from ADOPT-001 §12.7.8. WP-SCP-020 §4.1 follow-up; track parallel to 020H.1.' — no strikethrough, no '✅ landed' annotation. The established backlog-completion convention is '~~text~~ ✅ landed [date] (PR #N, commit sha)' — used for 020E.b, 020E.c, 020F, 020G, 020H part 3, 020H.2 (line 132). ADOPT-001 §12.7.8 was also updated in fix-round-1 to drop 'when published' and reference SECURITY.md directly — confirming the deliverable is live.","impact":"A reader of STATUS.md would incorrectly conclude SECURITY.md has not been published and SCP-073.sec remains pending. This misrepresents the deliverable status in the governance audit trail. The SCP-073.sec item says 'track parallel to 020H.1' — since 020H.1 is IN FLIGHT (this PR) and SECURITY.md was added in this same PR's fix-round-1, the parallel track is closed within this slice and should be recorded. Adopter-facing impact: an adopter reading STATUS.md to assess which ADOPT-001 §12.7 forward-looking flags have landed would conclude §12.7.8 is still a placeholder.","mitigation":"Update STATUS.md SCP-073.sec entry to: '~~**SCP-073.sec**: `SECURITY.md` publication (security disclosure path for policy-bypass reports) — referenced from ADOPT-001 §12.7.8. WP-SCP-020 §4.1 follow-up; track parallel to 020H.1.~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (fix-round-1 commit `3817384`); closes WP-SCP-020 §4.1 SCP-073.sec forward-looking flag; ADOPT-001 §12.7.8 updated.' before merge."},{"id":"COMP-R2-MIN-003","severity":"MIN","claim":"D-036 is absent from ADOPT-001 §12.7 References block, breaking the established per-slice D-NNN citation pattern — D-029 through D-035 (7 consecutive entries) are listed; D-036, the 020H.1 ratifying decision, is not.","evidence":"ADOPT-001 §12.7 References block (as read): 'docs/DECISIONS.md D-022 (federation-primitive adoption); D-029 (`statuses: write` for readback); D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection); D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account); D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-check); D-033 (rendered context-name `policy-check / scp/policy-check`); D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection); D-035 (020G adopter-helper invocation).' D-036 not listed. D-036 ratifies the versioning contract (relevant to §12.7.11 freshness warning and §12.7.7 SCP-FRESH-001 row) and the rule-RFC process (relevant to the overall federation-primitive governance shape described in §12.7). Prior slices 020B.1 → 020G each had their ratifying D-NNN appended to this block at merge time.","impact":"Adopters reading ADOPT-001 §12.7 for governance context behind the federation primitive's versioning behaviour and rule governance process cannot find the ratifying decision without scanning all of DECISIONS.md. Breaks the per-slice D-NNN citation pattern established across the entire §12.7 appendix. Minor navigability degradation; no functional impact on the gate.","mitigation":"Append 'D-036 (VERSIONING.md semver contract + rule-RFC process as estate doctrine; closes 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5)' to the docs/DECISIONS.md citation line in ADOPT-001 §12.7 References before merge."},{"id":"COMP-R2-nit-001","severity":"nit","claim":"TF-020H1-005 description in STATUS.md says 'Closure path: a follow-up edit adding §10 guidance on how to mark questions as blocking vs deferrable' — language that implies the primary fix is still pending — when RULE-TEMPLATE.md §10 was already updated in fix-round-1 (SAFE-nit-008). The TF is open only for future §10 enhancements.","evidence":"STATUS.md TF-020H1-005 (line 112): 'Closure path: a follow-up edit adding §10 guidance on how to mark questions as blocking vs deferrable. No deadline (cosmetic). Filed at 020H.1 R1 safety SAFE-nit-008 closure.' RULE-TEMPLATE.md §10 (as read, lines 145-162): '[BLOCKING] vs [deferrable] markers and explicit note that proposals with unresolved [BLOCKING] questions do NOT meet quorum, even with one CODEOWNER approval. Closes 020H.1 R1 SAFE-nit-008.' DISPATCH-NOTE TF-020H1-005 entry: 'RULE-TEMPLATE.md §10 BLOCKING-vs-deferrable guidance closed in fix-round-1; this TF tracks any subsequent §10 enhancement.' The DISPATCH-NOTE correctly characterises the item but STATUS.md does not.","impact":"A future slice author scanning STATUS.md open TF items would find TF-020H1-005 describing work that has already been done, potentially triggering wasted investigation. Cosmetic only; no governance gap.","mitigation":"Update TF-020H1-005 STATUS.md description to: 'RULE-TEMPLATE.md §10 [BLOCKING]/[deferrable] question-marking guidance and no-quorum-with-unresolved-BLOCKING note closed in fix-round-1 (SAFE-nit-008). This TF remains open only for any subsequent §10 refinement beyond what was added. No deadline (cosmetic).'"},{"id":"COMP-R2-nit-002","severity":"nit","claim":"DECISIONS.md 'Last Updated' header still reads 2026-04-30 after D-036 was filed on 2026-05-01, leaving the header one day behind the most recent entry.","evidence":"docs/DECISIONS.md line 3: '**Last Updated:** 2026-04-30'. D-036 row date field: '2026-05-01'. The header convention across the file is to reflect the date of the most recent D-NNN entry.","impact":"Cosmetic — the header is a human-readable datestamp, not machine-parseable. No functional impact on governance.","mitigation":"Update docs/DECISIONS.md header from '**Last Updated:** 2026-04-30' to '**Last Updated:** 2026-05-01'."}]}
